The solutions constructed above live at critical regularity and therefore satisfy (1) and (2) with equality. One may easily verify that for any $p \in [2,+\infty]$, $k \geq 0$, and $t \in (0,e^T)$, we have

$$t^{\frac{k}{2}} \| \nabla^k \bar  u(\cdot, t) \|_{L^p} + t^{\frac{k}{2}} \| \nabla^k  u(\cdot, t)  \|_{L^p} \lesssim_k t^{\frac{1}{2} (\frac{3}{p}-1)} \, , \tag{16}$$

$$t^{\frac{k}{2}} \| \nabla^k f(\cdot, t)\|_{L^p} 
        \lesssim_k t^{\frac{1}{2} (\frac{3}{p} - 3)}
         \, . \tag{17}$$

Our solutions moreover do not break the axisymmetric without swirl structure. However, it is likely that our instability does break the following *nearly* symmetric structure inherited from Vishik’s vortex. Namely, in two dimensions, Vishik’s instability breaks radial symmetry, retaining only strict $m$-fold rotational symmetry (see (18) below). The cross section of our vortex ring is nearly radial, and although we do not prove it, our unstable direction is likely nearly $m$-fold symmetric but not nearly radial. It is further striking that non-uniqueness holds already in this class because initially smooth axisymmetric solutions without swirl are known to remain globally smooth [36]. This suggests that non-uniqueness and finite-time singularity are separate issues, though in models exhibiting both, the two issues may be related through the problem of continuation past the singularity.

The standard estimate for the Biot-Savart kernel in $\mathbb{R}^3$, read on axisymmetric functions, gives us that

$$\| {\rm BS}_\ell[\omega]\|_{L^{6}((r+\ell)\,dr\,dz)} 
\lesssim\| \omega \|_{L^2((r+\ell)\,dr\,dz)} 
\lesssim\ell^{1/2}  \| \omega \|_{L^2(\gamma\,dr\,dz)} \, . \tag{58}$$

Hence, we estimate

$$\begin{split}
\| (r+\ell)^{-1} {\rm BS}_{\ell}[\omega]^r \widetilde{\omega}_\ell \|_{ L^2_{\gamma, \ell}} 
& =
\| (r+\ell)^{-1} {\rm BS}_{\ell}[\omega]^r \widetilde{\omega}_\ell \|_{ L^2(B_{\bar{R}})} 
\\& \lesssim
\frac 1 {\ell-\bar R} \|  {\rm BS}_{\ell}[\omega]\|_{ L^6(B_{\bar{R}})}  \| \widetilde{\omega}_\ell \|_{ L^3(B_{\bar{R}})} 
\\& \lesssim
\ell^{-5/6} \| {\rm BS}_{\ell}[\omega]\|_{ L^6((r+\ell)\,dr\,dz)}  \| \widetilde{\omega}_\ell \|_{ L^3(B_{\bar{R}})} 
\\& \lesssim
\ell^{-1/3} \| \omega \|_{L^2_{\gamma,\ell}} \| \widetilde{\omega}_\ell \|_{ L^3(B_{\bar{R}})}  \, .
\end{split} \tag{59}$$
